{
  "id": "10004",
  "key": "CL-4",
  "self": "https://your-domain.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/CL-4",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "Account security for contacts",
    "issuetype": {
      "name": "Story"
    },
    "status": {
      "name": "Ready for QA"
    },
    "priority": {
      "name": "High"
    },
    "labels": [
      "heldout-fail"
    ],
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Contact data is personal data. Every contacts endpoint must only work for a signed-in user, signing out must really end the session, and a user must never see or touch another user's contacts. Session tokens are issued by "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "POST /users",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " (sign-up) and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "POST /users/login",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and are sent as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Authorization: Bearer <token>",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Contacts carry an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "owner",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " field with the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "_id",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " of the user they belong to; the user's own "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "_id",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is returned by sign-up, sign-in and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "GET /users/me",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The acceptance criteria are written as scenarios; the tag on each scenario is its acceptance-criterion id."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "codeBlock",
          "attrs": {
            "language": "gherkin"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Feature: Account security for contacts\n\n  Background:\n    Given user \"A\" and user \"B\" have each signed up with their own unique e-mail address\n    And user \"A\" has a contact \"Secret Sam\" created with POST /contacts\n\n  @AC-1\n  Scenario Outline: Contacts endpoints require a session token\n    When a client calls <method> <path> without an Authorization header\n    Then the response status is 401\n    And the response body is {\"error\": \"Please authenticate.\"}\n    And no contact is created, changed or deleted\n\n    Examples:\n      | method | path                            |\n      | GET    | /contacts                       |\n      | POST   | /contacts                       |\n      | GET    | /contacts/{id of Secret Sam}    |\n      | PUT    | /contacts/{id of Secret Sam}    |\n      | PATCH  | /contacts/{id of Secret Sam}    |\n      | DELETE | /contacts/{id of Secret Sam}    |\n\n  @AC-2\n  Scenario: A token that was not issued by the application is refused\n    When a client calls GET /contacts with \"Authorization: Bearer\" followed by a made-up or altered token\n    Then the response status is 401\n    And the response body is {\"error\": \"Please authenticate.\"}\n\n  @AC-3\n  Scenario: Signing out ends the session\n    Given user \"A\" holds a token that returns A's contacts on GET /contacts\n    When user \"A\" calls POST /users/logout with that token\n    Then the response status is 200\n    And GET /contacts with the same token answers 401\n    And GET /users/me with the same token answers 401\n\n  @AC-4\n  Scenario: A user cannot read another user's contact\n    When user \"B\" calls GET /contacts/{id of Secret Sam}\n    Then the response status is 404\n    And GET /contacts for user \"B\" does not contain \"Secret Sam\"\n\n  @AC-5\n  Scenario Outline: A user cannot change or delete another user's contact\n    When user \"B\" calls <method> /contacts/{id of Secret Sam} with a valid body\n    Then the response status is 404\n    And GET /contacts/{id of Secret Sam} for user \"A\" still returns \"Secret Sam\" unchanged\n\n    Examples:\n      | method |\n      | PUT    |\n      | PATCH  |\n      | DELETE |\n\n  @AC-6\n  Scenario: A new contact always belongs to its creator\n    When user \"A\" calls POST /contacts with a valid body that also contains \"owner\" set to the _id of user \"B\"\n    Then the response status is 201\n    And the new contact's \"owner\" is the _id of user \"A\"\n    And the new contact is listed for user \"A\" and not for user \"B\"\n\n  @AC-7\n  Scenario Outline: The owner of an existing contact cannot be changed\n    When user \"A\" calls <method> /contacts/{id of Secret Sam} with a body that sets \"owner\" to the _id of user \"B\"\n    Then the request is either rejected with 400 or answered 200 with \"owner\" still the _id of user \"A\"\n    And GET /contacts/{id of Secret Sam} for user \"A\" still answers 200\n    And GET /contacts for user \"B\" does not contain \"Secret Sam\"\n\n    Examples:\n      | method | body                                                        |\n      | PUT    | first name, last name and owner                             |\n      | PATCH  | owner only                                                  |\n\n  @AC-8\n  Scenario: The contact list page only shows the signed-in user's contacts\n    Given user \"B\" has a contact \"Bella Bee\"\n    When user \"B\" signs in on the login page\n    Then the Contact List page shows \"Bella Bee\"\n    And it does not show \"Secret Sam\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Test data"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No accounts are provided: create users \"A\" and \"B\" through sign-up ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "POST /users",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ") with unique e-mail addresses, using the password from the environment variable "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "CL_USER_PASSWORD",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " for both. Delete both users afterwards with "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DELETE /users/me",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " where possible."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
